            ['title' => 'Where people get this wrong', 'html' => <<<'TXT'
            <ul><li><strong>Subtracting the years.</strong> 2010 minus 1990 is twenty, and the age was twenty only because the birthday had already passed.</li><li><strong>Treating the month line as calendar months.</strong> It is days since the last birthday over an average month, which is why the day line can differ from a hand count by one.</li><li><strong>A unit typed into the wrong box.</strong> Each box carries its own unit beside it. Mixing minutes with hours, or centimetres with inches, still produces a number that looks reasonable.</li><li><strong>A copied answer used as an input.</strong> The result boxes cannot be typed into, so a previous answer has to go back through the inputs to be reused.</li></ul>
